 "text": "Pork (pig meat) production in China, 1961–2024 | Husfarm\n\n# Pork (pig meat) production in China\n\nIn 2024 China produced 57.1 million t of pork (pig meat), the largest total in the world (45.5% of the world total). Over ten years it grew by 0.6%. The record was 57.9 million t in 2023. \n\nProduction, 2024\n\n57.1 million t\n\nWorld rank\n\n1 of 171\n\n10-year change\n\n+0.6%\n\nRecord\n\n57.9 million t\n\n2023\n\n## By year\n\n| Year | Tonnes | Change |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 2024 | 57,060,000 | −1.5% |\n| 2023 | 57,943,200 | +4.6% |\n| 2022 | 55,414,300 | +4.6% |\n| 2021 | 52,959,300 | +29% |\n| 2020 | 41,133,300 | −3.3% |\n| 2019 | 42,553,071 | −21% |\n| 2018 | 54,037,357 | −0.9% |\n| 2017 | 54,517,969 | +0.5% |\n| 2016 | 54,255,000 | −3.9% |\n| 2015 | 56,454,000 | −0.5% |\n| 2014 | 56,713,900 | +3.2% |\n| 2013 | 54,930,300 | +2.8% |\n| 2012 | 53,427,000 | +5.6% |\n| 2011 | 50,604,000 | −0.2% |\n| 2010 | 50,712,400 | +3.7% |\n| 2009 | 48,907,600 | +5.8% |\n| 2008 | 46,205,000 | +7.8% |\n| 2007 | 42,878,200 | −7.8% |\n| 2006 | 46,504,500 | +2.1% |\n| 2005 | 45,553,300 | +4.9% |\n| 2004 | 43,410,000 | +2.4% |\n| 2003 | 42,386,000 | +2.8% |\n| 2002 | 41,231,000 | +1.8% |\n| 2001 | 40,517,000 | +2.2% |\n| 2000 | 39,659,900 | −1.0% |\n| 1999 | 40,056,000 | +3.1% |\n| 1998 | 38,837,000 | +8.0% |\n| 1997 | 35,963,000 | +14% |\n| 1996 | 31,580,000 | −13% |\n| 1995 | 36,483,700 | +14% |\n| 1994 | 32,048,300 | +12% |\n| 1993 | 28,544,000 | +8.3% |\n| 1992 | 26,353,000 | +7.5% |\n| 1991 | 24,523,000 | +9.7% |\n| 1990 | 22,354,800 | +6.4% |\n| 1989 | 21,015,720 | +5.2% |\n| 1988 | 19,974,250 | +8.9% |\n| 1987 | 18,349,008 | +6.9% |\n| 1986 | 17,167,000 | +3.7% |\n| 1985 | 16,547,000 | +15% |\n| 1984 | 14,447,000 | +9.8% |\n| 1983 | 13,161,000 | +3.5% |\n| 1982 | 12,718,000 | +7.0% |\n| 1981 | 11,884,000 | +4.8% |\n| 1980 | 11,341,000 | +13% |\n| 1979 | 10,015,000 | +24% |\n| 1978 | 8,048,000 | +10% |\n| 1977 | 7,300,000 | −0.4% |\n| 1976 | 7,330,000 | −1.7% |\n|